Subject: [PATCH] book ch.11: non-orthogonal factorial ANOVA (unbalanced_anova)

- Orthogonality check (Eq. 11.1) with replication tables for every pair.
- Sequential (Type I) tables in the given and reverse order, Type II SS;
  SS and df from rank-based nested least-squares fits, so empty cells give
  correct interaction df.
- Backward selection respecting marginality; block and an extraneous factor
  are fitted first and never dropped.
- Predictions from the final model: cell table and marginal tables with equal
  weights, SE and SED from the parameter covariance, non-estimable cells
  flagged; optional Healy-Westmacott comparison table.
- Tests against Tables 11.13, 11.15, 11.17, 11.18, 11.20, 11.23, 11.24.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
